+# Age-Restricted Products Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Add store-wide age-restriction policy, private customer birthdays, server-side purchase enforcement, and supporting Dashboard/storefront experiences.
+
+**Architecture:** Typed fields on `Product`, `User`, and `SiteSettings` define policy and personal data. A shared backend eligibility service performs the calendar calculation and is called before checkout or draft-order completion side effects. GraphQL resolvers and mutation cleaners enforce birthday privacy and authorization; Dashboard and storefront consume only the data they need.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Django/Python/Graphene/PostgreSQL; React/TypeScript/Apollo; Next.js/GraphQL code generation; pytest and frontend test runners.
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-28-age-restricted-products-design.md`
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- Restricted products remain visible in every catalog context; buying, not visibility, is restricted.
+- The store-wide minimum age is a positive integer, defaults to `18`, and applies to all later checks.
+- Use Saleor's configured Django `TIME_ZONE` as the shop time zone; compare dates, not times.
+- A 29 February birthday reaches its anniversary on 1 March in a non-leap year.
+- Only a customer reading/updating their own account and a superuser reading/updating a customer may access birthday data.
+- Never expose birthdays in public APIs/profiles, unauthenticated responses, webhooks, or exports.
+- Audit every birthday write and every superuser birthday read without storing the birthday value in audit-event parameters.
+- Enforce `checkoutComplete` and `draftOrderComplete`; allow unlinked drafts; leave `orderBulkCreate` exempt.
+- Do not add dependencies, do not commit or push, and leave changes in the working trees.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+- A signed-in customer attempts to query another customer's birthday: return no birthday and create no read event.
+- An app impersonating a customer tries to update or read a birthday: reject it even with `IMPERSONATE_USER`.
+- A checkout's customer changes after its lines are built: enforce against the customer resolved at final completion, not cached storefront state.
+- The store minimum age changes between cart display and completion: use the value loaded at completion, not the label's cached value.
+- A checkout error is retried after sign-in/profile update: preserve the cart and permit a newly eligible customer to complete normally.
+
+---
